@startuml
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "User App" as Client
participant "API Gateway\n(Kong)" as Gateway
participant "Payment Service\n(Go)" as PaymentSvc
participant "Redis Cluster" as Redis
participant "Fraud Service" as FraudSvc
participant "Apache Kafka" as Kafka
participant "Saga Orchestrator" as Orchestrator
database "CockroachDB\n(Sharded)" as DB
participant "Notification Service" as Notify

== Step 1: Ingress & Validation ==
Client -> Gateway: POST /v1/payments (Idempotency-Key, JWT, Payload)
Gateway -> Gateway: Validate TLS, JWT & Token Bucket Rate Limit
Gateway -> PaymentSvc: Forward authorized request

== Step 2: Idempotency & Pre-flight Checks ==
PaymentSvc -> Redis: SETNX idempotency:{key} PENDING EX 86400
alt Key Already Exists (Duplicate Retry)
    Redis --> PaymentSvc: Exists (Return cached response or In-Flight)
    PaymentSvc --> Client: 200 OK (Previous Result) / 409 Conflict
end
Redis --> PaymentSvc: Key Acquired (OK)

PaymentSvc -> FraudSvc: Validate Risk (sync SLA < 15ms)
alt Fraud Rule Breached
    FraudSvc --> PaymentSvc: REJECTED (High Risk)
    PaymentSvc -> DB: Log Failed Transaction (REJECTED_FRAUD)
    PaymentSvc --> Client: 403 Forbidden (Fraud Check Failed)
end
FraudSvc --> PaymentSvc: APPROVED

== Step 3: Event Ingestion (Outbox Pattern) ==
PaymentSvc -> Kafka: Publish 'txn.initiated' (account_id key)
Kafka --> PaymentSvc: ACK (acks=all)
PaymentSvc --> Client: 202 Accepted (Transaction In-Process, txn_id)

== Step 4: Saga Execution & Balance Updates ==
Kafka -> Orchestrator: Consume 'txn.initiated'
Orchestrator -> DB: Begin Distributed Sub-Transaction
Orchestrator -> DB: Debit Sender (OCC: version = version + 1 WHERE balance >= amount)
alt Insufficient Balance / Version Mismatch
    DB --> Orchestrator: Abort (Zero Rows Affected)
    Orchestrator -> Kafka: Publish 'txn.failed' (Reason: Insufficient Balance)
    Kafka -> Notify: Trigger Failure Push/SMS
else Debit Succeeded
    DB --> Orchestrator: Debit Confirmed
    Orchestrator -> DB: Credit Receiver (version = version + 1)
    Orchestrator -> DB: Insert Double-Entry Ledger Records
    DB --> Orchestrator: Commit Succeeded
    Orchestrator -> Kafka: Publish 'txn.completed'
    Kafka -> Notify: Push Success Event to Client & Receiver
end
@enduml